{{also|émulsion|emulsión|Emulsion}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|émulsion|notext=1}}, from {{etyl|NL.|en}} {{m|la|ēmulsiō|ēmulsiō, ēmulsiōnis}}, based on {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ēmulgeō||I milk out, extract}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# a [[stable]] [[suspension]] of small [[droplet]]s of one [[liquid]] in another with which it is [[immiscible]]
#: ''Mayonnaise is an '''emulsion''' where egg is used to keep oil and water mixed.''
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} a [[colloid]] in which both [[phase]]s are liquid
# the coating of [[photosensitive]] [[silver]] [[halide]] grains in a thin [[gelatine]] [[layer]] on a [[photographic]] [[film]]

